    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **46 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp33Tests`, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the no-future-date rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`). When a request supplies a `registrationDate` that is later than the server date, the create is rejected with **400 Bad Request**:\n\n```java\njava.time.LocalDate serverDate = java.time.LocalDate.now();\nif (owner.getRegistrationDate() != null && owner.getRegistrationDate().isAfter(serverDate)) {\n    throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST,\n        \"Registration date must not be later than the current server date\");\n}\n```\n\nKey design points:\n- The check runs on the **supplied** date, before the business-day roll \u2014 so it doesn't interact with weekend/holiday rolling (Cp07/Cp20 still pass).\n- Only a supplied date is validated; a `null` (defaulted) date is unaffected, and the server date itself is captured once and reused for defaulting.\n- `isAfter` means \"strictly later than,\" so a same-day registration is still accepted.\n\nThe whole suite (all Cp01\u2013Cp33 acceptance tests) passes.",
